Package: FESV
Type: Package
Title: Fixed Effects Covariate Selection Using Shapley Values
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Htwe", "Ko", email = "htwe_k@cmu.ac.th", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A cooperative game-theoretic framework for covariate selection in
    two-way fixed effects panel data models. Candidate covariates are treated
    as players in a coalitional game whose characteristic function is the
    improvement in a penalised goodness-of-fit statistic (adjusted R^2 by
    default) relative to the fixed-effects-only baseline. The Shapley value
    allocates each covariate's average marginal contribution across all
    coalitions and provides two data-driven selection rules: (A) a positive
    Shapley value and (B) a nested penalised criterion J(k) = v(M_k) - gamma*k.
    The package provides exact enumeration for small covariate sets, Monte
    Carlo permutation sampling for larger sets, residual-bootstrap inference,
    fixed-effects OLS on selected coalitions, game-theoretic diagnostics, and
    selection metrics. The method is fully frequentist.
